l production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. Post-rollback: all regions on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate 0.2%. Follow-up: root-cause the v2.3.1 regression before re-deploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56422, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011u7NeBccdUAysoyint4Z4z", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_not_found", "safe_retry_with_key", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56422, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011u7NeBccdUAysoyint4Z4z", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60288, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. The service was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy. The two later ones, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, are both marked unhealthy.\n- **After:** All three regions are on v2.3.0 and pass health checks, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** It covers the failure, the rollback and the post-rollback numbers, plus a follow-up to find the cause of the v2.3.1 failure before anyone deploys it again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LtE2rwzPskP74UgjyeA2AB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017GJtdDMAzarHZoJH